ivates them  all a glance at the specs reveals that  even after downsizing from a six to a  four cylinder engine the volvo xc90  still got plenty of power  the t6 we tested sends 235 kilowatts to  its all-wheel drive propelling the  vehicles two tons from zero to a hundred  kilometers per hour in six and a half  seconds technology tester sasha knopf  checked out the safety features  he says the new xc90 has made some  advances in terms of safety it's got for  instance a new driver's assist that  senses if the car runs off the road this  isn't a lane departure warning it  actually works passively it activates an  electronic belt tightener that keeps the  seat belt firmly tightened during an  accident he says many other systems use  a pressurized gas chamber  once it's empty the tension on the seat  belt lets up very rapidly but this  electronic belt tightener keeps the  tension up the entire time the vehicle  is  runoff road protection is standard on  the new xc90 the moment the sensors  detect the car leaving the asphalt the  front seat belts are tightened  electronically as far as they'll go and  kept that way until the vehicle comes to  a standstill  sasha says he's also had the opportunity  to drive the xc90s t8 version which is  the plug-in hybrid it puts out 294  kilowatts of power but carries a hefty  price tag over 76 000 euros for that it  promises both sportiness and  environmental friendliness now he's  going to take a look  the t8 is the top of the line xc90 with  just two and a half liters of fuel per  100 kilometers this beefy suv puts out  294 kilowatts of power but produces just  59 grams of co2 per kilometer  a touch of class in the interior is the  shift lever made of crystal glass  design tester tanju gench sums up  the xc90 has evolved the front is new  but the rear is typical for volvo he  liked the design but not the price but  at least he gets something good for the  money  the suv meets everyone's needs looks  good and offers the safety features  expected of oval and what's sasha knop's  impression  he says the xc60 was the best-selling  mid-range suv in 2014 and this new xc90  met all his expectations all in all he  thinks things are looking up for volvo  and the run-up to the unveiling ceremony  for its new rs ford ruled out the red  carpet for the cars forbearers  visitors to the car makers facility in  cologne loved it  the first rs was built in cologne says  stila merka the car maker launched the  15 mrs and the 17 mrs in 1967.  telos club is happy to have the chance  to present cars from the model's history  the first of those two models featured a  55 kilowatt 1.7 liter engine with a  paint job sporting racing stripes  but it was body details in the 17 mrs  that would define the special model's  look its standard v6 engine packs 66  kilowatts of power but customers could  also opt for a racier 79 kilowatt  version  inside the dash and dials emphasize the  car's sporty image  says the first motors were powerful but  conventional later ford introduced turbo  engines fuel injection and four-wheel  drive special rally racing technologies  and ford brought them to the street  the brand first brought out a street  legal rally style car in the 1960s  because of its grill the escort rs was  fondly known as the dog  bone the rs 200 was an extreme example  of ford's technology transfer developed  for group b rally races its huge air  intake scoops fed a mid-mounted engine  what rule changes force designers to  return to more conventional vehicles the  focus became a rally car but even the  street legal rs pulled a respectable 154  kilowatts out of four cylinders its  successor also a front-wheel drive  vehicle was a real eye-catcher drivers  could call audits up to 500 newton  meters of torque when necessary  amateur racer frog freudzime says this  car still has its original five-cylinder  motor and to handle it you have to watch  the rpms and torque that means you can  either torque it up close to the red  line or shift early and pick up speed  through torque when you accelerate  ford started the countdown to the  official launch of the latest generation  rs with a surprise appearance the  prototype was piloted over the  carmaker's factory grounds by rally  racer and internet phenomenon ken block  on the way to the presentation it was  his job to show off how well the car  handles even when pushed to the limit by  maneuvering past some expensive  obstacles  it was a final test for the new rs which  looks set to find a new fan base outside  the sport as well guests were impressed  the pro was too  well i mean i'm very happy that ford uh  has developed you know the rs again  brought the heritage back to the rs  brand uh but on top of that developing  it with all-wheel drive and more  horsepower uh you know than they have in  the past is amazing so it's been really  cool to be a part of the development  process on such a very good car  the audience got a look at what the new  top of the line focus can do but only  saw the final design after it had been  put through its paces that's when ford  pulled off the wrapping paper on the new  compact made in cologne  the look is radical for the car maker  ford design manager ernesto rupar says  the focus rs was developed here in  cologne but the overall design was a  joint effort with the ford performance  team in detroit  performance is everything in the compact  sports car segment cooling aerodynamics  and technology have to be top notch  the model's head engineer says its motor  which is the same as the mustangs has a  2.3 liter ecoboost it's been  fundamentally altered and adapted in the  rs it was implemented in conjunction  with the all-wheel drive of course he  says  that ladder feature appears to have been  made for ken block's extreme driving  style he's glad ford has implemented the  change  so i've been pushing that for that for  years and uh ford really listened and  and listened to not only me though but  the customers that the customers wanted  that too  so  really you know that initial development  of the all-wheel drive and the idea that  was uh something i i was able to help  with  and since then i've been able to  help with the  you know the testing and tuning of the  uh the all-wheel drive system and the  suspension so that's mainly what i've  been involved with  in combination with the car maker's  torque vectoring technology the  all-wheel drive can distribute up to 70  percent of the engine's 235 kilowatts of  output to the rear wheels and up to 100  percent of that to the outside wheel in  a curve so lateral acceleration of up to  1g poses no problem  hungry fans will have to be patient  though it's still unclear exactly when  the new rs will hit the market  mercedes is adding sporty amg models to  its c-class stable top of the line is  the c63 amg powered by a 350 kilowatt v8  engine  the s version boasts 25 kilowatts more  power  other special features include an amg  sports suspension with three-stage  adjustable damping and a locking rear  differential  the leon st cooper is seatt's sporty new  station wagon the model is available  with a choice of 195 or 206 kilowatt  engines when fitted with the heftier  power plant the leon st cupra can charge  from zero to 100 kilometers an hour in  just six seconds yet the car also offers  a generous  1470 liters of cargo space  car tester chris kestia says this is a  very special golf the e-golf with  electric drive only it has no  gasoline-powered engine so it isn't a  hybrid he's going to be testing the car  in ice and snow  the volkswagen golf has been a fixture  on streets the world over for 40 years  now but this is the first purely  electric model and it completes the car  makers range of powertrains  many other car makers developed their  electric vehicles as separate models and  built them in separate plants but not vw  the e-golf looks just like a  conventional golf and it's produced  right alongside its gasoline-powered  piers in wolfsburg  chris says the e-golf is a proper golf  it's just as uncluttered and spacious as  the gasoline-powered models the only  difference is in the dashboard display  which is of course geared to electric  drive  the electric gulf's interior is  virtually identical to that of a  conventional gulf  under the hood the electric motor hums  along  depending on the route driving style  load and outside temperature the e-golf  can range between 130 and  kilometers on a charge the electric  motor achieves 85 kilowatts and a  maximum 270 newton meters of torque  right from a standstill and his  performance on the road is quite  satisfactory there are no gears the  motor accelerates evenly up to its 140  kilometer an hour limit  chris points out another big advantage  of the electric vw the trunk is spacious  the cargo space's 305 liters is just as  much as in the gasoline and  diesel-powered golf models  that's because the batteries are built  into the floor and tunnel  and when the driver hits the brakes the  electric motor recuperates energy and  recharges the batteries  different settings or regen levels are  available to determine how much the  motor can be used to break the car  a gauge in the cockpit tells the driver  exactly how much energy is flowing back  into the batteries  three driver selectable levels  coordinate the interaction of the motor  and the braking system  chris confirms that even at below  freezing the e-golf has a good range in  the eco plus mode more than 130  kilometers per charge  it may look like a regular golf on the  outside but the inside is packed with  high-tech only a few details on the body  betray its presence  the shuttered blue striped grille and  especially designed rims identify the  e-golf streamline the vehicle to  increase range  the e-golf can be connected to any  outlet  and it can be recharged to eighty  percent capacity at public charging  stations in 30 minutes  chris sums up that with a relatively  limited range of 150 kilometers the  e-golf is best suited to urban driving  this is for car shoppers looking for an  emissions free and comfortable ride but  at a starting price of 35 000 euros it's  not the cheapest  spring is in the air the perfect season  for bmw to launch the successor to its  one series convertible the two series  convertible is just over seven  centimeters longer than its predecessor  but it's retained the brand's typical  proportions with little overhang a long  hood long wheelbase and broad toe  product manager paloma schmidt brakling  says what really sets the car apart from  its forebear is the discrete design  larger dimensions and enhanced luxury  the silhouette is longer with flat  shoulders and a very small rear that's  why it handles great and looks so sporty  she says even when parked  since its introduction in 2008 130 000  units of the one series compact  convertible have been sold the 2 series  convertible is flatter and longer than  the 1 series 3 and 5 door models  roll bars are hidden inside the  headrests and back and a new  construction material has gone into the  car's retractable roof  paloma says bmw was able to reduce  ambient noise by five to seven decibels  by adding insulation  the soft top can be opened and closed in  just 20 seconds at speeds up to 50  kilometers an hour  so you don't have to pull over just to  put the top up or down a nice feature it  means you can react almost instantly to  sudden changes in weather with the top  down the new model also has 20 more  liters of volume in the trunk than its  predecessor for more cargo space owners  can lower the rear seats  our test car was fitted with the brand  sportline interior it includes accents  like red seats red seams on the steering  wheel and red highlights on the door  panels  customers can also choose from the  advantage luxury line or m sport  packages  our car sports the 228i inline  four-cylinder gasoline engine that packs  180 kilowatts the automatic transmission  eases up to 100 kilometers an hour in  six seconds and top speed of  250. the new 2-series convertible has  already gone on sale in german  dealerships now the weather just has to  play along  classic cars always turn heads  most people love to look at vintage  vehicles and a lucky few have the  pleasure of owning one  but even fewer drive theirs around every  day and draw plenty of envious glances  guy newmark from california is one of  those lucky people for close to half a  century he's been tooling around in this  1964 porsche  356c porsche  that uh my family's owned almost since  new  my dad got it uh  i guess  about  a month  after it was brought here to the united  states then he drove it for  three or four years  and gave it to me when i graduated from  college and we've been inseparable  everywhere i go i'm with blue  blue isn't just any old car it's guy  newmark's constant companion  blue has a  900 about 992 000 miles now  um  when i received blue it had a little  under 80 000. my dad had put that on it  76 or 77 thousand and i put all the rest  on  twenty thousand  miles a year that i put on the car  before taking over his father's yacht  business guy was his dad's right hand  man  back in the days before email and fax  machines guy had to travel to his  customers to do business  sometimes he drove clear across the u s  it was then that he developed his close  relationship with blue  and the car has held a special place in  his heart to this day  i love the color  the color is just magnificent it's bali  blue it's original porsche color we  haven't changed it at all  and  the other  thing is that when you're driving a 356  uh you're really driving a car  there's no special handling there's no  uh  you know gift of any mechanical you're  you're driving a car and when i talk to  people that have driven 356s  and they've sold them  every person 100 have said i'm really  sorry i sold my 356 because it's such an  exhilarating driving experience  since 1971 blue has shared the garage  with another porsche 356 a red 1962  convertible but blue remains guy's  favorite  so it's the original engine we've  rebuilt it twice  and matter of fact this last month we  just did valves and  went through the engine cad plated  everything we did rings new muffler and  blue's ready for another million miles  now  i think the secret is wonderful  engineering  um  and that combined with  proper maintenance  it is a mechanical item you do have to  maintain it and i'm pretty religious  about  changing the oil and taking care of it  and having the valves adjusted  another secret to blue's longevity is  the magnet affixed to the oil filter it  catches any metal particles that pass  through the filter and prevents them  from entering the engine compartment  guy also had the interior completely  refurbished although that was over  twenty five years ago  everything was restored to its original  condition  only the lamb's wool seat covers are the  owner's private touch  the old 356 seize odometer only goes up  to 99  999 miles but guy plans to be driving  blue for a long while to come  blue's a buddy  i've been living with blue for almost 50  years so blue blue's a friend i talk to  blue all the time i just i'm in real  trouble if blue talks back to me  he loves the porsche but guy hasn't  always been faithful  well i bought another car  and i bought that car so i wouldn't have  to drive blue every day in case it was  raining or i just didn't want to drive  blue and the very first day i drove that  car on the freeway i was rear-ended and  pushed into the back of a truck and the  car was totaled  and i think it was blue saying what the  hell are you doing  and so i would drive blue every day  wherever i go no matter what the weather  is  blue's odometer shows that the porsche  has so far traveled 990  823 miles or around 1 594  575 kilometers  that's the equivalent of rounding the  globe almost forty times or traveling to  the moon and back twice  the car still has nine thousand miles to  go to crack the million mark but after  fifty years on the road blue is still  going strong and shows no sign of  slowing down  next time on drive it join us as we  check out skoda's new fabia station  wagon  and see what's new for spring at the  geneva motor show  you

