smission  eases up to 100 kilometers an hour in  six seconds and top speed of  250. the new 2-series convertible has  already gone on sale in german  dealerships now the weather just has to  play along  classic cars always turn heads  most people love to look at vintage  vehicles and a lucky few have the  pleasure of owning one  but even fewer drive theirs around every  day and draw plenty of envious glances  guy newmark from california is one of  those lucky people for close to half a  century he's been tooling around in this  1964 porsche  356c porsche  that uh my family's owned almost since  new  my dad got it uh  i guess  about  a month  after it was brought here to the united  states then he drove it for  three or four years  and gave it to me when i graduated from  college and we've been inseparable  everywhere i go i'm with blue  blue isn't just any old car it's guy  newmark's constant companion  blue has a  900 about 992 000 miles now  um  when i received blue it had a little  under 80 000. my dad had put that on it  76 or 77 thousand and i put all the rest  on  twenty thousand  miles a year that i put on the car  before taking over his father's yacht  business guy was his dad's right hand  man  back in the days before email and fax  machines guy had to travel to his  customers to do business  sometimes he drove clear across the u s  it was then that he developed his close  relationship with blue  and the car has held a special place in  his heart to this day  i love the color  the color is just magnificent it's bali  blue it's original porsche color we  haven't changed it at all  and  the other  thing is that when you're driving a 356  uh you're really driving a car  there's no special handling there's no  uh  you know gift of any mechanical you're  you're driving a car and when i talk to  people that have driven 356s  and they've sold them  every person 100 have said i'm really  sorry i sold my 356 because it's such an  exhilarating driving experience  since 1971 blue has shared the garage  with another porsche 356 a red 1962  convertible but blue remains guy's  favorite  so it's the original engine we've  rebuilt it twice  and matter of fact this last month we  just did valves and  went through the engine cad plated  everything we did rings new muffler and  blue's ready for another million miles  now  i think the secret is wonderful  engineering  um  and that combined with  proper maintenance  it is a mechanical item you do have to  maintain it and i'm pretty religious  about  changing the oil and taking care of it  and having the valves adjusted  another secret to blue's longevity is  the magnet affixed to the oil filter it  catches any metal particles that pass  through the filter and prevents them  from entering the engine compartment  guy also had the interior completely  refurbished although that was over  twenty five years ago  everything was restored to its original  condition  only the lamb's wool seat covers are the  owner's private touch  the old 356 seize odometer only goes up  to 99  999 miles but guy plans to be driving  blue for a long while to come  blue's a buddy  i've been living with blue for almost 50  years so blue blue's a friend i talk to  blue all the time i just i'm in real  trouble if blue talks back to me  he loves the porsche but guy hasn't  always been faithful  well i bought another car  and i bought that car so i wouldn't have  to drive blue every day in case it was  raining or i just didn't want to drive  blue and the very first day i drove that  car on the freeway i was rear-ended and  pushed into the back of a truck and the  car was totaled  and i think it was blue saying what the  hell are you doing  and so i would drive blue every day  wherever i go no matter what the weather  is  blue's odometer shows that the porsche  has so far traveled 990  823 miles or around 1 594  575 kilometers  that's the equivalent of rounding the  globe almost forty times or traveling to  the moon and back twice  the car still has nine thousand miles to  go to crack the million mark but after  fifty years on the road blue is still  going strong and shows no sign of  slowing down  next time on drive it join us as we  check out skoda's new fabia station  wagon  and see what's new for spring at the  geneva motor show  you
 

